 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? It depends on the type of oil and the intensity of the piece. A general rule is six months for a plain oil painting. Then let it dry completely, with a light coat of wax or clear gloss to seal it. That'll keep it safe enough for a few days. A quick wipe with a dry cloth is all you need. It'll feel slightly tacky to the fingertip. The paint will still feel soft. It'll take a full six months in a well ventilated spot.",
